Subject: [PATCH] [mlir][bytecode] Number nested attributes and types from a worklist

`IRNumberingState::number` numbers an attribute or type by a dummy
writing whose `writeAttribute` and `writeType` number each nested
component as they are reached, so numbering calls itself, through the
dialect's bytecode interface, once per level of nesting: writing a
builtin array nested a few thousand deep, or a long chain of call-site
locations, needs a native stack that grows with the depth of the IR. The
dummy writer now records the components it reaches (nested attributes
and types, referenced resources, and a callback's group name), and they
are numbered afterwards from an explicit stack: the components of a newly
numbered value before the rest of the components reached with it. This
is the order the recursion took, so values, dialects and resources are
numbered, and the bytecode written, exactly as before.
---
